# 2️⃣ Query Optimization Basics

Now important real-world thinking.

---

## Big Idea

Optimization means:

```text id="mt9l5j"
Get result using minimum time/resources
```

---

# Why Optimization Matters

Small data:

```text id="9gbtqy"
Slow query acceptable
```

Millions of rows:

```text id="x0u6aa"
Slow query = disaster ❌
```

---

# Common Optimization Ideas

---

## 🔹 Use Indexes

Without index:

Database scans every row.

```text id="nt8w3s"
O(n)
```

With index:

Fast lookup.

---

### Example

```sql id="v4u5mv"
CREATE INDEX idx_name ON students(name);
```

---

## 🔹 Avoid SELECT *

Bad:

```sql id="78wz2n"
SELECT * FROM students;
```

Why bad?

* Fetches unnecessary columns
* More memory
* More network cost

---

Better:

```sql id="vxgq2s"
SELECT name, marks FROM students;
```

---

## Mental Model

```text id="cgw0h6"
Take only what you need
```

---

## 🔹 Filter Early

Good:

```sql id="k6s6kz"
SELECT name
FROM students
WHERE branch='CSE';
```

Database filters first → less processing.

---

## 🔹 Use LIMIT When Needed

Bad:

```sql id="o5y6k5"
SELECT * FROM logs;
```

Huge data.

Better:

```sql id="h5d74v"
SELECT * FROM logs LIMIT 10;
```

---

## 🔹 Avoid Unnecessary Joins

More joins = more processing.

Only join needed tables.

---

# Full Table Scan

## Simple Idea

Database checks every row.

Very slow on large data.

---

## Happens When

* No index
* Bad filtering
* Function on indexed column

---

## Example

Bad:

```sql id="lfjzwj"
WHERE YEAR(date)=2025
```

May ignore index.

Better:

```sql id="8emc7z"
WHERE date BETWEEN '2025-01-01' AND '2025-12-31'
```

---

# Query Execution Plan

Databases internally create a plan:

```text id="1j8mb3"
How to access table
Which index to use
Join order
Filtering strategy
```

Interviewers love this topic.

---

# Memory Tricks 🧠

```text id="evr4np"
Optimization = less work

Indexes = shortcuts

SELECT * = usually bad
```

